---
import Icon from '../system/components/Icon.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import MediaText from '../system/blocks/Media/Text.astro';
import Facilities from '../components/CardSlider.astro';
import { portalHref } from '../config/integrations';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

// Same applicant registration the homepage hero points at.
const applyHref = portalHref('entrance') ?? '/admissions';
const applyAttrs = applyHref.startsWith('http') ? { rel: 'noopener' } : {};
import introPhoto from '../assets/images/classroom.png';
import libraryPhoto from '../assets/images/library.png';

// Four stage cards across, so each one is roughly a quarter of the container
// rather than the third the three-card layouts elsewhere ask for.
const cardSizes = '(max-width: 820px) 92vw, (max-width: 1080px) 46vw, 23vw';

// The four stages, in order. A school running three stages, or six, adds or
// removes a Markdown file; the grid class below already adapts.
const programmes = (await getCollection('programmes')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---
<Layout
  title={`Academics-${site.name}`}
  description="The Nigerian national curriculum at Unifac Group of Schools: nursery, primary, junior and senior secondary, taught across three campuses in Benin City."
  active="academics"
>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Academics</p>
    <h1>One path, from the first day to the final certificate.</h1>
    <p>The Nigerian national curriculum at every stage, from the pre-primary years through Primary 1 to 6, then JSS 1 to 3 for the Basic Education Certificate and SSS 1 to 3 for the WASSCE and NECO examinations.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<MediaText
  image={introPhoto}
  alt="Learners in a bright classroom"
  eyebrow="Our Approach"
  title="How a lesson runs here."
>
  <p>Lessons follow the national scheme of work term by term, and it is the same scheme on all three campuses. Written work is marked against the standard of the examination a pupil is heading for rather than the one they sat last, so a JSS 1 script is judged by where it is going.</p>
  <p>Standards on their own produce a good script and not necessarily a good person. We pair them with what the crest already claims: honesty, punctuality, and finishing what you have started.</p>
</MediaText>

<section class="academics">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Our Programmes</p><h2>Every stage, thoughtfully designed.</h2><p>Four connected stages that carry each child from playful early learning to confident, examination-ready study.</p></div>
    <div class={`prog${programmes.length === 4 ? ' four' : ''}`}>
      {programmes.map((programme) => (
        <div class="pcard has-media">
          <div class="pcard-media"><Image src={programme.data.cover} alt={programme.data.coverAlt} widths={[400, 640, 900]} sizes={cardSizes} format="webp" quality={72} loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="pcard-in"><div class="age">{programme.data.stage}</div><h3>{programme.data.title}</h3><p>{programme.data.summary}</p></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<MediaText
  image={libraryPhoto}
  alt="The school library"
  eyebrow="Beyond the Textbook"
  title="A curriculum that goes further."
  reverse={true}
  surface="alt"
>
  <p>A timetable says when a subject is taught. It does not say whether a child has understood it, and the part of this school that matters most is the hour after a lesson, when the pupil who did not follow it says so and is taken back through it.</p>
  <p>Music, art, computer studies and sport are taught rather than left to chance, each in a room meant for it.</p>
  <p>Assessments and lessons are moving online through ResultPeak and JDSmartLearn. Both are being set up for Unifac now, so the <a href="/portal">portal pages</a> describe what is coming and link nowhere until the sign-in is genuinely ready.</p>
</MediaText>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Why {site.shortName}</p><h2>How we teach.</h2><p>Three things we hold to, on all three campuses.</p></div>
    <div class="feat-grid">
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><Icon name="book" /></div>
        <h3>The National Curriculum, Taught Fully</h3>
        <p>The BECE at the end of JSS 3, the WASSCE and NECO at the end of SSS 3. The certificates a Nigerian university asks for, taught to the national syllabus.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><Icon name="users" /></div>
        <h3>Three Campuses, One Standard</h3>
        <p>Whichever campus a child sits on, the syllabus, the terms and the examinations are the same. A family moving between them loses nothing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><Icon name="shield-check" /></div>
        <h3>Strong Pastoral Care</h3>
        <p>We know each learner as an individual, supporting wellbeing and character alongside academic progress.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Facilities
  surface="alt"
  title="Learning you can put your hands on."
  intro="A syllabus is only half of it. These are the rooms where the practical papers get practised and the reading gets done."
/>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--accent-300)">Admissions Open</p>
    <h2>Find the right stage for your child.</h2>
    <p>Tell us the year group you have in mind and we will tell you what is available, on which campus.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-gold btn-lg" href={applyHref} {...applyAttrs}>Apply for a Place <span class="arr">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/contact">Ask a Question</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
